    "ordering": "Seed and freeze balanced random order within phase/window, honoring cache-treatment setup and dependencies. Do not reorder based on observed speed.",
    "identity": "Scenario, template, seed, group, session, turn, request, source/config/model/region/reasoning/affinity/connection settings must be explicit. Repeated logical template is not repeated trial identity.",
    "stop": "Stop on invalid evidence, exceeded limits, manifest drift, secret leak, cancellation or provider rate-limit exhaustion; preserve partial results. A genuine endpoint error remains an outcome. No retry/replacement. No output-cap escalation.",
    "censoring": "Record censoring as a measured session/workload outcome; preserve latency bounds and all denominators. It is not an automatic abort for this newly defined descriptive program. Unknown finish metadata invalidates evidence.",
    "qualification": "No endpoint-qualified or universal capacity/fixed-cap feasibility claim. Only empirical finite-sample characterization; no invented SLOs.",
    "time": "Temporal anchor chosen only when released; scheduled windows never overlap. Record delays/misses; do not backfill. No new persistent OS/app scheduler.",
